content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-111 – AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-21100",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration 4.2 mm/s against HF-300 Figure 3 severity zones: Zone A 0–2.8, Zone B 2.8–4.5 (long-term operation), Zone C 4.5–7.1 (restricted – plan maintenance), Zone D >7.1 (stop the pump). 4.2 mm/s is in Zone B, only 0.3 mm/s below the Zone C boundary. This does not by itself require a stop. Figure 3 applies to the highest reading taken on either bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing housing temperature 74 C against the manual limits: normal up to 70 C, alarm 80 C, trip 90 C. 74 C is 4 C above normal and 6 C below alarm. This is abnormal but not an alarm or trip condition. The limits apply to the housing surface.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Grinding noise from the non-drive-end bearing (6310-C3, HF3-510) indicates bearing wear. Manual 5.3 requires both bearings to be replaced as a pair when either shows wear, noise or high temperature. Both noise and above-normal temperature are present.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The report says the seal is dry. If this means no leakage at the shaft seal, it is acceptable. If it means the seal is running without flush, it breaches the manual requirement: Plan 11 flush from pump discharge, never run dry. This must be confirmed on arrival.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Non-drive-end bearing wear or damage. Grinding noise, raised housing temperature and elevated vibration together match the bearing wear cause listed for both high vibration and high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment. It is listed as a cause of high vibration, high bearing temperature and seal problems, and may have caused or accelerated the bearing wear.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing of the bearings, listed as a cause of high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage, or cavitation, listed as further causes of high vibration. These are less likely given that the noise is localised at the NDE bearing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Loss of seal flush (seal run dry), if 'seal is dry' means the flush is absent. This is a cause of seal face damage.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "On arrival, before any other work, confirm the seal condition and that Plan 11 flush from pump discharge is flowing. The manual says never run dry. If the seal is running without flush, stop the pump immediately rather than waiting for the planned outage.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Take vibration readings on both bearing housings and a housing-surface temperature on both housings to confirm the trend. If vibration exceeds 4.5 mm/s (Zone C), maintenance is restricted and must be planned. Above 7.1 mm/s (Zone D), or at 90 C trip or above, stop the pump. Escalate at 80 C alarm.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly (68 kg; lifting equipment required). The casing and pipework stay in place.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Replace both bearings as a pair per manual 5.3: drive-end 6312-C3 (HF3-512) and non-drive-end 6310-C3 (HF3-510). Check the grease quantity, because over-greasing is a listed cause of high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C05",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "While the assembly is out, inspect the mechanical seal faces, the shaft sleeve (for scoring) and the impeller. If the seal is worn or cracked, or ran dry, replace it per manual 5.2 with component seal HF3-450, NOT HF3-450B. Remove the impeller nut and impeller, withdraw the seal and sleeve, inspect the sleeve, then fit the new seal.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09",
        "C13",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit a new casing gasket HF3-120 on reassembly; it must be replaced whenever the casing is opened.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reinstall the back pull-out assembly. Tighten all fasteners, including the seal gland, to manual Table 5. This pump is below serial HF3-22000, so the bulletin's 30 Nm gland torque does not apply. The Table 5 values are not in the evidence provided and must be obtained before work starts.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Carry out laser shaft alignment, because the work moved the bearing housing. Tolerances: parallel offset 0.05 mm; angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Restore the Plan 11 seal flush before start-up. After restart, record vibration on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading per Figure 3; the target is Zone A or B. Confirm housing temperature is at or below 70 C normal.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3 (replace as pair)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3 (replace as pair)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket – replace whenever casing is opened",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450",
      "description": "Mechanical seal, component type – carry as standby; fit if inspection shows wear or dry-running damage (correct part for serial below HF3-22000)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve – carry as standby; fit if sleeve is scored on inspection",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate (lock out) and drain the pump before dismantling.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg; use lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Do not run the pump with the seal dry; confirm the Plan 11 flush before any restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Stop criteria while the pump remains in service: vibration in Zone D (>7.1 mm/s) or housing temperature at the 90 C trip. Escalate at the 80 C alarm or on entering Zone C (>4.5 mm/s).",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement (pair): 6.0 h, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 h, 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement, if required after inspection: 4.0 h, 2 technicians. Some overlap with bearing work is possible, since both use back pull-out removal.",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Service bulletin SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) supersedes seal HF3-450 with cartridge seal HF3-450B and changes the gland torque to 30 Nm (was 25 Nm). The bulletin applies only to serial HF3-22000 and above. P-111 is serial HF3-21100, below that range. The bulletin states that such pumps continue to use HF3-450 and Table 5 of the manual. Decision: use manual part HF3-450 and Table 5 torques; do not fit HF3-450B or use 30 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The bulletin's sleeve replacement criterion (scoring over 0.1 mm depth) and its 'no sleeve measurement needed' note apply only to HF3-450B pumps at serial HF3-22000 and above. For this pump, manual 5.2 applies: inspect the sleeve for scoring. The manual gives no numerical limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Manual Table 5 fastener and seal gland torque values are not in the evidence provided. The bulletin implies the old gland torque was 25 Nm, but Table 5 should be obtained and confirmed before reassembly.",
    "Does 'seal is dry' mean no leakage (acceptable) or that the seal flush has been lost and the seal is running dry (stop required)?",
    "Which housing gave the 4.2 mm/s reading? Was it measured as RMS velocity? Was the 74 C reading taken on the NDE or DE housing surface?",
    "The manual excerpt gives no detailed bearing removal and fitting procedure, bearing grease type or grease quantity.",
    "The manual gives no numerical sleeve scoring rejection limit for pumps below serial HF3-22000.",
    "There is no vibration or temperature trend history to show how fast the condition is deteriorating, so the time available before Zone C or the 80 C alarm is unknown."
  ]
}
